#DESCRIPTION
Free-stream (uniform-equilibrium) regression test of the FULL PIC
electromagnetic field solver (implicit Maxwell/GMRES): solveEM=T,
useHybridPIC=F.

The initial condition is a perfectly uniform plasma (zero bulk velocity,
uniform guide field Bx0) -- the exact steady solution -- so any growth of
non-uniform structure indicates a solver bug.  The hybrid Hall-OFF counterpart
(PARAM.in.hybrid) shares the identical grid, plasma, normalization,
timestepping, and output, differing only in the field-solver block.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Full PIC electromagnetic field solver ON (implicit Maxwell/GMRES); the
Hybrid-PIC Ohm's-law solver is OFF. The two are mutually exclusive.
#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

The implicit GMRES solver advances E and B with the displacement current, so it
is not limited by an explicit light-speed CFL; no Hall sub-cycling is needed.
#DIVE
F                       doCorrectDivE
3                       nDivECorrection

#EFIELDSOLVER
1.0e-8                  tol        GMRES relative tolerance
30                      nIter      GMRES max iterations

Field time-discretization for the implicit Maxwell solver (theta-scheme).
theta = 1 is fully implicit, 0.5 is Crank-Nicolson. coefDiff is the
diffusion coefficient (0 = none).
#DISCRETIZATION
0.5                     theta
0.0                     coefDiff

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nS
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    npcelx
1                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
10.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
